# Scripts are checked out with LF on every platform.
#
# A test imports scripts/espn-canary.mjs, and under CRLF (a default Windows
# checkout) the test transform has failed on that file twice: a `#!` line it did
# not strip, and a stall on line comments that hold quote characters (no test
# file ever finished, and the CI job ran to its time limit). Node itself runs
# either form. This takes the difference away.
scripts/** text eol=lf
